<section image-layout="blank" id="cLCtn87nOc"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="jPfzkGcBON" vertical-align="center" colspan="36"><p role="eyebrow">Illustrative replacement · 12 ha field</p><h1 font-size="46pt">Five hours are hiding in the field</h1><p font-size="lg">At 2.0 m and 5.0 km/h, 70% field efficiency turns a theoretical 12.00-hour job into 17.14 hours of work.</p><p role="eyebrow">12 ha time ledger</p><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="j92SNizWFh" background-color="surface" padding="14pt 16pt" colspan="42"><display size="md">12.00<span font-size="18pt"> h</span></display><h4>Theoretical work time</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="f9Tc0U4dEk" background-color="accent" padding="14pt 16pt" colspan="18"><display size="md">5.14<span font-size="18pt"> h</span></display><h4>Field-loss time</h4></grid-item></grid><grid divider="sm neutral-border" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="AmqtddgU7_" colspan="30"><h3>1.00 ha/hour</h3><p>Theoretical capacity before field losses.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="v90pTIuC2A" colspan="30"><h3><span text-color="accent">0.70 ha/hour</span></h3><p>Effective capacity at 70% efficiency.</p></grid-item></grid><p font-size="12pt"><span text-color="muted">The source document was not supplied; all examples in this deck are created and illustrative.</span></p></grid-item><grid-item id="yfwgVSha_0" padding="0" colspan="24"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/QWf0hE26o8zs8fyLshCqG.png" saved-media-id="mgmujrrp5hvers2" source="image.ai-generated" fill="true" image-style="technical-field-documentary" alt="Elevated documentary photograph of an unbranded compact tractor working a rectangular cultivated field, parallel passes and a broad headland clearly visible, neutral overcast daylight, realistic soil texture, carbon-black and machine-gray equipment with one restrained signal-red marker, no text, no logos, no identifiable people" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="7bHrCxXJRG"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="TU7Y--B-hM"><h2>Three numbers define field efficiency</h2><p font-size="lg">The recurring example starts with three operating inputs. Keep their units fixed and enter efficiency as a decimal.</p><grid divider="sm neutral-border" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="i4uPHpeWEh" vertical-align="center" colspan="20"><display size="md">2.0<span font-size="20pt"> m</span></display><h4>Working width</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="kUsimZOQCz" vertical-align="center" colspan="20"><display size="md">5.0<span font-size="20pt"> km/h</span></display><h4>Operating speed</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="ysJ4ZjS3sV" vertical-align="center" colspan="20"><display size="md"><span text-color="accent">0.70</span></display><h4>Field efficiency</h4></grid-item></grid><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="ocr1kI96Mq" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><h3>Capacity ladder</h3><p role="eyebrow">Theoretical capacity</p><formula>C_t=\frac{2.0\times5.0}{10}=1.00\ \text{ha/hour}</formula><p role="eyebrow">Effective capacity</p><formula>C_e=C_t\times0.70=0.70\ \text{ha/hour}</formula></grid-item><grid-item id="6NFDkfAgt8" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><h3>Losses become cost</h3><formula>\eta_f=\frac{C_e}{C_t}=0.70</formula><p>Field efficiency captures turning, overlap, refilling, adjustment and stoppage losses.</p><formula>\frac{\$54/\text{hour}}{0.70\ \text{ha/hour}}=\$77.14/\text{ha}</formula></grid-item></grid><p font-size="12pt"><span text-color="muted">Field-capacity method:</span> <a href="https://www.extension.iastate.edu/agdm/crops/html/a3-24.html">Iowa State University Extension, Ag Decision Maker A3-24</a> · $54/hour is an illustrative input.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="zZB1kjz0C4"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="7eYzNhFwdR"><p role="eyebrow">One field · five control points</p><h2>Efficiency is won before, during and after the pass</h2><p font-size="lg">Each stage produces a decision or record that prevents a different source of lost time or poor work quality.</p><grid marker="number" marker-rule="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-gap: 0.6em;"><grid-item id="frX5rY5EuR" colspan="12"><h3>Plan</h3><p>Map field shape, access and the work window. Produce a route sketch.</p><labels><label variant="outline">TURN LOSS</label></labels></grid-item><grid-item id="7AEiIhFq-w" colspan="12"><h3>Select</h3><p>Match implement, power and expected annual use.</p><labels><label variant="outline">SYSTEM MISMATCH</label></labels></grid-item><grid-item id="DrRZP5_LM-" colspan="12"><h3>Set up</h3><p>Calibrate width, depth, pressure and input delivery.</p><labels><label variant="outline">OVERLAP + MISSES</label></labels></grid-item><grid-item id="W0aAKJZsGO" colspan="12"><h3>Operate</h3><p>Record speed, turns, refill time and stoppages.</p><labels><label variant="outline">WAITING LOSS</label></labels></grid-item><grid-item id="chZDKDkLY6" colspan="12"><h3>Verify</h3><p>Inspect quality, log the result and correct the next run.</p><labels><label variant="outline">REPEAT LOSS</label></labels></grid-item></grid><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="enkkTdCZnn" background-color="accent" padding="14pt 18pt"><h3>Field efficiency is not a machine specification—it is the cumulative result of these five controls.</h3></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="slf79en9Qj"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="_-YedioLbd"><p role="eyebrow">Illustrative options · same field task</p><h2>Select the system, not the biggest machine</h2><p font-size="lg">The schematic compares pass count across the same 12 m swath. Capacity and cost improve only if the wider system also fits the tractor, field and work standard.</p><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="UAE08YXnQd" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><labels><label variant="outline">OPTION A</label></labels><h3>2.0 m system</h3><grid spacing="small"><grid-item id="tO1OUQ8uDD" background-color="palette-3" padding="0" colspan="10"><p></p></grid-item><grid-item id="2n1ODfGiCz" background-color="palette-3" padding="0" colspan="10"><p></p></grid-item><grid-item id="RkB0_iJGRy" background-color="palette-3" padding="0" colspan="10"><p></p></grid-item><grid-item id="R9aH37beoM" background-color="palette-3" padding="0" colspan="10"><p></p></grid-item><grid-item id="eGVFSFP9jn" background-color="palette-3" padding="0" colspan="10"><p></p></grid-item><grid-item id="mMDcZBZOY-" background-color="palette-3" padding="0" colspan="10"><p></p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">Six 2.0 m passes across the schematic swath.</p><formula>2.0\times5.0\times0.70\div10=0.70\ \text{ha/hour}</formula><display size="md">$77.14<span font-size="18pt">/ha</span></display><formula>\$54/\text{hour}\div0.70=\$77.14/\text{ha}</formula></grid-item><grid-item id="Zb-c5zav0K" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><labels><label variant="solid">OPTION B · CONDITIONAL</label></labels><h3>3.0 m system</h3><grid spacing="small"><grid-item id="y7WN0iSXoP" background-color="accent" padding="0" colspan="15"><p></p></grid-item><grid-item id="5PJ2YLLrhR" background-color="accent" padding="0" colspan="15"><p></p></grid-item><grid-item id="0GIsHu_tAW" background-color="accent" padding="0" colspan="15"><p></p></grid-item><grid-item id="K4hyPzl-ES" background-color="accent" padding="0" colspan="15"><p></p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">Four 3.0 m passes across the schematic swath.</p><formula>3.0\times6.0\times0.75\div10=1.35\ \text{ha/hour}</formula><display size="md">$57.78<span font-size="18pt">/ha</span></display><formula>\$78/\text{hour}\div1.35=\$57.78/\text{ha}</formula></grid-item></grid><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="P4IPH4o9gM" background-color="accent" padding="12pt 16pt"><p><b>Decision gate:</b> verify power and hitch · soil load and work quality · transport width and access · annual utilization.</p></grid-item></grid><p font-size="12pt"><span text-color="muted">Pass diagram is schematic, not a plan of the full 12 ha field. Operating speed must remain compatible with soil and work-quality requirements.</span></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="AfZ89A3Jod" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="o8wl1mkOnd"><p role="eyebrow">Illustrative calculation · 12 ha · USD</p><h2>Reproduce the calculation</h2><p font-size="lg">Follow the units through each link. The effective capacity calculated in step three becomes the denominator for both cost figures.</p><grid marker="number" marker-rule="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-gap: 0.6em;"><grid-item id="3ArsRtp0x6" colspan="15"><h4>State the inputs</h4><p>Width 2.0 m; speed 5.0 km/h; efficiency 0.70; hourly cost $54.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="nM6KrQnELI" colspan="15"><h4>Find theoretical capacity</h4><formula>C_t=2.0\times5.0\div10=1.00</formula><p>ha/hour before field losses.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="1kHpsaGXQZ" colspan="15"><h4>Apply field efficiency</h4><formula>C_e=1.00\times0.70=0.70</formula><p>ha/hour effective capacity.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="vWBfIBT-cV" colspan="15"><h4>Convert capacity to cost</h4><formula>54\div0.70=77.14</formula><p>$77.14/ha</p><formula>54\times12\div0.70=925.71</formula><p>$925.71 for 12 ha.</p></grid-item></grid><p font-size="12pt"><span text-color="muted">Cost-method reference:</span> <a href="https://www.extension.iastate.edu/agdm/crops/html/a3-29.html">Iowa State University Extension, Ag Decision Maker A3-29</a> · Illustrative USD; excludes taxes, financing terms, subsidies and policy effects.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="bE2cdYSGd-"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="4efX5HBpDy"><h2>Turn measured losses into actions</h2><p>Start with the observed signal, verify its cause, then change the part of the system that created the loss.</p><table col-widths="[23,35,42]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false"><tbody><tr><td background-color="surface"><p>Measured signal</p></td><td background-color="surface"><p>Verify the cause</p></td><td background-color="surface"><p>Action</p></td></tr><tr><td valign="middle"><p><span text-color="accent"><b>Low field efficiency</b></span></p></td><td valign="middle"><p>Time turns and refills.</p></td><td valign="middle"><p>Redesign routes and stage inputs before work begins.</p></td></tr><tr><td valign="middle"><p><span text-color="accent"><b>Low capacity</b></span></p></td><td valign="middle"><p>Check actual speed, working width and available power.</p></td><td valign="middle"><p>Correct the limiting mismatch; do not raise speed if quality or soil conditions deteriorate.</p></td></tr><tr><td valign="middle"><p><span text-color="accent"><b>High cost/ha</b></span></p></td><td valign="middle"><p>Inspect idle time, fuel, repairs and annual utilization.</p></td><td valign="middle"><p>Reduce avoidable idle hours and match ownership or hire cost to expected use.</p></td></tr><tr><td valign="middle"><p><span text-color="accent"><b>Poor work quality</b></span></p></td><td valign="middle"><p>Measure overlap, misses and depth.</p></td><td valign="middle"><p>Calibrate before increasing speed or capacity.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="sEfAIvfS9d" background-color="accent" padding="12pt 16pt"><p><b>Track together:</b> ha/hour, field efficiency, cost/ha, fuel/ha, downtime and work quality.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="-JNzizJ6IZ"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="ZRN3WYNYWl" padding="0" colspan="18"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/DhXm_2dZxwf7I543zrOu8.png" saved-media-id="uy5fwwdz6qhg3dg" source="image.ai-generated" fill="true" image-style="technical-field-documentary" alt="Elevated documentary photograph of an unbranded tractor approaching a field headland where inputs, tools and a support trailer have been staged in an orderly sequence, short turning path and reduced waiting geometry clearly visible, neutral overcast daylight, realistic soil texture, machine-gray equipment with restrained signal-red route markers, no text, no logos, no identifiable people" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item><grid-item id="9Rq0031qou" padding="32pt 38pt" colspan="42"><p role="eyebrow">Illustrative case study · same 12 ha field</p><h2>Remove waiting before adding power</h2><p>Better headland routing and staged inputs raise assumed field efficiency while width, speed and hourly machine cost remain unchanged.</p><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="0YoAz9EpCO" background-color="surface" vertical-align="center" padding="16pt 18pt" colspan="22"><p font-size="34pt"><b>0.70 → </b><span text-color="accent"><b>0.82</b></span></p><h4>Field efficiency</h4><p>Same 2.0 m width, 5.0 km/h speed and $54/hour cost.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="i-Z-mBtnVH" vertical-align="center" colspan="38"><h4>Hours required for 12 ha</h4><graph chart-type="bar" show-data-labels="true" y-axis-min="0" text-size="md" config="{&quot;appearance&quot;:{&quot;customSeriesColors&quot;:{&quot;series1&quot;:{&quot;color&quot;:&quot;#C51D2A&quot;},&quot;series2&quot;:{&quot;color&quot;:&quot;#4E5965&quot;}}},&quot;legend&quot;:{&quot;position&quot;:&quot;none&quot;}}" width="260pt" height="105pt"><properties><property key="scenario" label="Scenario" type="label"></property><property key="hours" label="Hours for 12 ha" type="data"></property></properties><data><row><cell>Before</cell><cell>17.14</cell></row><row><cell>After</cell><cell>14.63</cell></row></data></graph></grid-item></grid><grid divider="sm neutral-border" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="V2FEOWvzoM" colspan="30"><h4>Cost per hectare</h4><p font-size="lg"><b>$77.14 → $65.85</b></p></grid-item><grid-item id="k98vcddEb-" colspan="30"><h4>Total for 12 ha</h4><p font-size="lg"><b>$925.71 → $790.24</b></p></grid-item></grid><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="bxiOhvjIWs" background-color="accent" padding="12pt 16pt"><h3>2.51 hours and $135.47 saved</h3><p>14.6% less time and cost. Assumes staging adds no hourly cost and work quality is unchanged.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="wxmMrlIVmL"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="m50kqibFy8"><p role="eyebrow">Operating standard</p><h1 font-size="38pt">Buy back minutes before buying more machine</h1><h3 role="subheading">First ask: which lost minute is cheapest to eliminate?</h3><grid marker="number" marker-style="solid" marker-shape="circle" marker-rule="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-gap: 0.6em;"><grid-item id="O3e9UnJs1p" colspan="12"><h3>Measure</h3><p font-size="18pt">Record effective ha/hour in real field conditions.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="FyvH8Qdg_N" colspan="12"><h3>Separate</h3><p font-size="18pt">Split turning, waiting, adjustment and stoppage minutes.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="SZ7dADG49b" colspan="12"><h3>Compare</h3><p font-size="18pt">Test viable systems in work-window hours and cost/ha.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="VAb-_jmRk2" colspan="12"><h3>Improve first</h3><p font-size="18pt">Fix routing, logistics, calibration and maintenance.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="TNS3lHPSyL" colspan="12"><h3>Remeasure</h3><p font-size="18pt">Check cost and work quality, then return to step 01.</p></grid-item></grid><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="aWNXCRMsKL" background-color="accent" vertical-align="center" padding="18pt" colspan="16"><p role="eyebrow">Decision gate</p><h2>ADD CAPACITY?</h2></grid-item><grid-item id="43v7uSD7Bh" background-color="surface" padding="18pt 22pt" colspan="44"><h3>Add capacity only if verified residual hours still miss the work window.</h3><p>Power, hitch, soil load, access, work quality and total cost must also remain acceptable.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>